# Strapi conventions

Each API under `src/api/<name>/` has `content-types/<name>/schema.json`, plus `controllers/`, `routes/`, `services/`. Prefer `createCoreRouter` / `createCoreController` unless customizing.

## Custom routes

Export `{ type: 'content-api', routes: [...] }` so paths mount under `/api`. Extra files in `routes/` (e.g. `custom-routes.js`) are also loaded.

## Relations (keep in sync)

- Project → contractors, approvers (project-team), tasks, project_inspections, HomeBuyer (user)
- Task → project, standard_task, contractor (M2M), sub_contractor, submissions, project_team_member
- Registration → sub_contractor, status pending/approved/rejected (onboarding, not Strapi users-permissions register)
- Submission → task, submitted_by, proofOfWork media, status pending/approved/rejected
- User → user_group → designation + access-control flags

## Known schema gaps

Task controller may set `assigned_date` (not on schema). User has no `contractor` relation though task code assumes it. Project documents component field is `document_code` (singular).
